@V := "tape" :: spec [active]
  version = "1.0"

@H 1175 := "SELECTION / fitness-differential reproduction — does Darwinian selection (fit cells divide more, unfit cull) produce evolution BEYOND instructive growth? (evolution MISSING #1: selection)" :: universe [🔴 CLOSED-NEGATIVE — selection adds nothing over instructive growth at toy scale]
  seed         = "Audit gap: anima has variation (daughter noise) + heredity (inherit centroid) + reproduction (mitosis) but NO SELECTION — every cell survives equally. Without fitness-differential survival there is no Darwinian evolution, only instructive/Lamarckian adaptation (H_1159). This is the keystone evolution gap."
  substrate    = "toy $0 CPU. REUSE h1159b cells on a fixed-capacity population; ADD fitness = inverse running error; fit cells divide MORE (reproduction prob ~ fitness), unfit cells are CULLED (needs 1171 apoptosis). Compare SELECTION arm vs instructive-growth-only (H_1159) arm."
  method       = "FROZEN FALSIFIER (pre-reg): 🟢 SELECTION-EVOLVES iff the selection arm's POPULATION mean-fitness INCREASES over generations and beats instructive-growth on a held-out shifted task (Cohen's d>=0.8) — i.e. differential reproduction adds adaptive power instruction alone lacks. 🔴 if selection adds nothing over instructive online-adaptation at toy scale (a_paper_negative_ok)."
  verdict_tier = "🔴 CLOSED-NEGATIVE (toy $0 numpy CPU, 8 seeds 900-907, deterministic, g5/p7, frozen pre-reg; a_paper_negative_ok). BOTH frozen gates FAIL. (A) population mean-fitness does NOT increase over 14 gens: mean dFit(late-early)=-0.0019, only 2/8 seeds increasing (<0.5 majority bar). (B) selection does NOT beat instructive on held-out SHIFTED task — it is WORSE: Cohen d(ins-sel)=-1.92 (selection heldout_err=10.96 > instructive 7.11). FINDING: the Darwinian cull-fittest/reproduce operator COLLAPSES cell diversity (fit parent's daughter overwrites the culled cell → population converges on the dominant-cluster centroid), HURTING generalization to a novel-but-related shifted world; the matched instructive arm (H_1159, every cell adapts equally, none replaced) keeps a more diverse spread that covers the shifted+new clusters better. At toy scale instructive/Lamarckian online-adaptation captures the available adaptive gains AND retains the diversity that differential reproduction destroys — selection is NOT a distinct adaptive lever here. Construction: CAP=12 fixed-capacity population, fitness=1/(1+running clustering-err) p7, held-out task=centers shifted N(0,2) + 2 genuinely-new clusters, both arms matched on cap/LR/stream/seed (only the selection operator differs). RUN VERIFIED deterministic-identical on re-run."
  scope        = "toy numpy $0 CPU prototype-cell PROXY for CORE cell-division; live engine + scale UNVERIFIED (a_scale_honest_scope). p7, fitness=substrate clustering error not perplexity."
  xref         = "h1159_inference_time_mitosis_learning · 1171_apoptosis_death · 1176_resource_competition · 1177_generations_population · p8"
